## Why This Is Asked
Assess the candidate’s ability to structure a practical CBA for a distributed architecture shift, weighing latency, privacy, and cost against risk reduction and retention gains.

## Key Concepts
- Edge computing vs centralized analytics
- Inference costs, device storage, data transfer
- Regulatory/compliance penalties and risk
- Uplift in fraud detection and user retention
- Break-even analysis and sensitivity testing

## Code Example
```javascript
function breakEven(initialCost, monthlySavings, monthlyCosts) {
  let months = 0;
  let net = -initialCost;
  while (net < 0) {
    net += (monthlySavings - monthlyCosts);
    months++;
  }
  return months;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you design the data governance model to satisfy privacy regulations across regions?
- What mitigation plans exist if edge devices underperform (false positives, latency spikes, battery impact)?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to scope CBAs for privacy-preserving on-device ML and quantify energy, storage, bandwidth, and compliance trade-offs.

## Key Concepts
- Federated learning
- Gradient compression
- Privacy/compliance overhead
- Cost modeling
- Rollout strategy

## Code Example
```javascript
function computeCBA(params){
  const {devices, energyPerDevice, uplink, cloud, retention} = params;
  const energy = devices * energyPerDevice;
  const total = energy + uplink + cloud + retention;
  const breakeven = total / Math.max(1, (params.revenuePerUser || 1));
  return {energy, total, breakeven};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle drift and model staleness in rollout?
- What metrics would you track to decide go/no-go, and how would you test them in a pilot?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a privacy-preserving, on-device ML feature with a clear financial rationale and real-world constraints.

## Key Concepts

- On-device ML size/latency trade-offs
- Energy, memory, and storage budgeting for mobile apps
- Telemetry costs and delta-based model updates
- Regulatory/compliance costs and risk assessment
- Go/no-go criteria and break-even planning

## Code Example

```javascript
function inferLeadScore(features, model) {
  // simple LR-like dot product
  let score = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < features.length; i++) {
    score += features[i] * model.weights[i];
  }
  return 1 / (1 + Math.exp(-score));
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate drift and schedule model updates offline?
- How would you audit privacy, regulatory compliance, and data minimization during rollout?

## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates the ability to translate a feature into a measurable business and engineering plan, focusing on CBA fundamentals, trade-offs, and governance for a client-side offline feature.

## Key Concepts

- **Client-side indexing and offline user experience**: Implementing lightweight search indexes (e.g., Lunr) for instant offline note search
- **Cost modeling**: Storage, CPU, latency, and privacy considerations
- **Rollout planning**: Phased deployment with validation metrics and maintenance scheduling

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple Lunr index search
const index = lunr(function() {
  this.field('title', { boost: 10 });
  this.field('content');
  this.ref('id');
});

documents.forEach(doc => index.add(doc));

const results = index.search('search term');
```

## Why This Is Asked

Gauges ability to justify product bets with a pragmatic, numbers-driven approach and to handle uncertainty in inputs.

## Key Concepts

- Cost estimation
- Benefit estimation
- Break-even analysis
- Reasonable assumptions

## Code Example

```javascript
// Simple CBA calculator
function cba(params) {
  const {maU, lift, arpu, months, cost} = params;
  const annualizedBenefit = maU * lift * arpu * months;
  return {annualizedBenefit, cost, breakevenMonths: cost / (annualizedBenefit || 1)};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adjust if MAU grows or adoption changes?
- What if ARPU uplift is not uniform across user segments?

## Why This Is Asked
CBA for an offline-first backup feature requires tangible cost knobs and measurable outcomes beyond accuracy or latency; beginner-friendly but demonstrates ability to quantify trade-offs and plan rollout.

## Key Concepts
- Energy budgeting per photo and dedup impact
- Data minimization and privacy/compliance
- Rollout, offline fallback, drift/maintenance, break-even

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo energy check before upload
function shouldUpload(photoSizeMB, currentEnergyJ, thresholdJ){
  const dedupFactor = 1.5;
  const energyPerMB = 0.25;
  const energy = photoSizeMB * energyPerMB * dedupFactor;
  return (currentEnergyJ - energy) > thresholdJ;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure de-dup effectiveness in production?
- What metrics trigger rollback during rollout?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to model privacy-preserving analytics, not ML, with real-world trade-offs across storage, compute, energy, and compliance.

## Key Concepts
- Privacy budgets & CRDTs for local aggregation
- Edge-resource constraints and telemetry design
- Compliance costs and regulatory penalties

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple CRDT-like Grow-Only Counter
class GCounter { constructor() { this.counters = new Map(); }
inc(k, v=1){ this.counters.set(k, Math.max((this.counters.get(k)||0)+v,0)); }
merge(other){ for(const [k,v] of other.counters){ this.counters.set(k, Math.max((this.counters.get(k)||0), v)); } }
value(){ let s=0; for(const v of this.counters.values()) s+=v; return s; }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you handle CRDT reconciliation when offline and merging after sync?
- What metrics would you track to detect drift in your aggregates and how would you price the analytics feature?

## Why This Is Asked

Assesses designing a privacy-conscious, on-device NLP feature with energy, storage, and regulatory constraints, plus a quantified cost-benefit trade-off.

## Key Concepts

- On-device ML and multilingual support
- Energy budgeting, latency targets, local storage planning
- Privacy budgets, regulatory/compliance costs, opt-in controls
- Staged rollout and metrics for go/no-go decisions

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo inference loop for on-device summarization
function summarize(conversation, model) {
  // assume preloaded model in memory
  const chunk = chunkify(conversation, 512);
  return chunk.map(c => model.infer(c)).join(" ");
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you validate privacy guarantees during updates?
- How would you measure missed insights vs. privacy budget over time?
